.TH ORBIS 1 "2026-09-08" "Orbis 0.1.0-beta.1.dev.1" "Orbis manual"
.SH NAME
orbis \- your Linux software, in one place
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B orbis
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Orbis is a Linux-first, provider-neutral interface for discovering software, explaining package metadata, reviewing transaction plans, and carrying out carefully confirmed package operations.
.PP
This is an early public Beta release. Orbis is safety-first but still evolving. Review every transaction plan before allowing package state to change.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Emit structured JSON instead of terminal presentation.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable ANSI styling.
.TP
.B --plain
Force the traditional terminal presentation.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print the Orbis version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B dashboard
Launch the interactive dashboard. \fBui\fR is an alias.
.TP
.B sources
Show detected providers and read-only capabilities.
.TP
.B search \fIQUERY\fR
Search available providers.
.TP
.B info \fIPACKAGE\fR
Show normalized package metadata.
.TP
.B explain \fIPACKAGE\fR
Explain a package in plain language.
.TP
.B doctor
Run safe provider and environment diagnostics.
.TP
.B install \fIPACKAGE\fR
Plan and, after confirmation, install one exact package.
.TP
.B remove \fIPACKAGE\fR
Plan and, after confirmation, remove one exact package without purge or autoremove.
.TP
.B update
Refresh package catalogs without upgrading installed software.
.TP
.B updates
Show installed software with updates available. Read-only.
.TP
.B upgrade
Plan and, after confirmation, apply safe available updates.
.TP
.B clean
Plan and, after confirmation, remove confidently unused package-manager artifacts.
.TP
.B history
Read sanitized Orbis transaction and maintenance history.
.TP
.B why \fIPACKAGE\fR
Explain why one installed package or ref is present.
.SH SAFETY
.B --plan
and
.B --dry-run
stop before execution. Without
.B --yes,
an actual operation requires an interactive terminal and an explicit confirmation. Administrator authorization is requested only for the exact system-scoped operation that has been reviewed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/orbis/transactions/
Sanitized transaction records.
.TP
.I $HOME/.local/state/orbis/transactions/
Fallback transaction-record directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt-get (8),
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR snap (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Aritra Saha
